# Beads Acceptance and Pipeline Beads

Use with `agent-pipeline.mdc` (seven studio roles) and `PIPELINE.md`.

## Acceptance tiers

Set label `acceptance:mechanical` or `acceptance:fuzzy` on the epic when
creating it. Default: `feature`/`epic` → fuzzy; `task`/`chore`/`bug` →
mechanical unless the acceptance criteria require player-visible judgment.

### Mechanical (single bead)

Use when every acceptance line is objectively verifiable (tests, lint,
CLI output, file exists).

- One bead. Implementer claims, implements, closes with evidence in `--notes`.
- Example notes: test command + pass summary, or `bd preflight --check` output.

### Fuzzy (implement + accept pair)

Use when acceptance depends on gameplay feel, UX, visuals, design fidelity,
or multi-step behavior screenshots cannot be reduced to one unit test.

Required shape:

```
epic (acceptance signals on --acceptance)
├── … pipeline stage beads (gd → sd → ga) as needed …
├── <title> — implement   label stage:gameplay-programmer
├── <title> — review      label stage:code-reviewer
├── <title> — fix         label stage:gameplay-fixer   (only if review fails)
└── <title> — accept      label stage:qa-playtester
```

Dependencies (child depends on parent):

```bash
bd dep add accept-bead implement-bead
bd dep add review-bead implement-bead
bd dep add fix-bead review-bead          # when needed
bd dep add accept-bead review-bead       # or accept-bead fix-bead after fix
bd dep add epic-bead accept-bead
```

**Close authority**

| Bead | Who closes | Evidence |
|------|------------|----------|
| implement | Gameplay Programmer (or Fixer) | Tests + handoff in notes |
| review | Code Reviewer | Pass/fail verdict in notes |
| fix | Gameplay Fixer | Regression tests in notes |
| accept | QA Playtester only | Scenario scripts + screenshots |
| epic | QA after accept closes, or orchestrator after human sign-off | Accept bead closed |

Implementer and reviewer must **not** close the epic or the accept bead.

## Pipeline stage labels

Label stage beads `stage:game-director`, `stage:systems-designer`,
`stage:gameplay-architect`, `stage:gameplay-programmer`, `stage:code-reviewer`,
`stage:gameplay-fixer`, `stage:qa-playtester`.

Spawn the matching `.cursor/agents/<role>.md` subagent for that stage. Each
stage closes its own bead and writes a structured handoff in `--notes`:

- Inputs used
- Artifacts produced
- Next handoff target
- Explicit non-goals

Do not append unbounded pipeline-run markdown files for new work; the bead
graph and stage notes are the source of truth.

## Bugs

File bugs as bd issues (`--type=bug`), not GitHub Issues. QA verifies fixes
against repro steps, then closes the bug bead. Link bugs to the feature epic
with `bd dep add` when discovered during pipeline work.

## Orchestrator context diet

When spawning a subagent, pass: bead id, acceptance criteria, prior stage
notes summary, and search results — not the full parent chat log.
